Lumen OS: keep a vendor eARC link next to CEC ARC, as the stock XGIMI frameworks do.

The XGIMI vendors have no Android eARC HAL: the vendor brings the eARC link up by itself and raises a TV event. The
stock framework of every XGIMI family (services.jar of G0082, G0111, G0130, G0148: AudioService seteARCStatus,
geteArcStatus, setCecStatus; HdmiCecLocalDeviceTv notifyArcStatusToAudioService) keeps the soundbar output from it:
the link coming up while CEC ARC is not established connects the HDMI ARC output, the link ending removes it, and
CEC ARC ending while the link is up keeps the output ("don't disconnect ARC while eARC mode"). Here the projector
app reports the link in Settings.Global lumen_vendor_earc (stock: XRMService on the vendor's event 11), the new
VendorEarc holds the two states on the HDMI service thread and sets sys.lumen.vendor_earc_glue=1 so the app stops
connecting the output itself.

RequestArcInitiationAction.ANSWER_TIMEOUT_MS: how long the TV waits for the answer to <Request ARC Initiation>.
It is HdmiConfig.TIMEOUT_MS, 2000 ms started before the request is sent: exactly what every stock XGIMI framework does
(services.jar RequestArcInitiationAction.start, const/16 2000 before sendCommand: G0082, G0148 6.17.12, X50 v1.3.38;
javac drops the other branch). A longer value would start the wait when the request was really sent.

The unpatched files are the LineageOS 21 sources of the shipped Lumen services.jar (same methods, references and
strings per class: cec-fix-1127 fw_cmp.py). Device-neutral: without the setting nothing changes.

